From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:06:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] SfxrInstance::resetSample: keep the period at least 8, as
 getAudio does

A looping sound restarts at its envelope's end through resetSample, which
set period = (int)fperiod: a base frequency past about 10 (damaged or
random settings) made it 0, and the next supersample's phase %= period
divided by zero. resetSample now bounds it at 8 as getAudio does. This
changes the rest of the restarting sample for periods of 1 to 7, which
getAudio then raised to 8 only from the next sample.
---
 src/audiosource/sfxr/soloud_sfxr.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/sfxr/soloud_sfxr.cpp b/src/audiosource/sfxr/soloud_sfxr.cpp
index e3455de..4ad5785 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/sfxr/soloud_sfxr.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/sfxr/soloud_sfxr.cpp
@@ -253,6 +253,9 @@ namespace SoLoud
 			phase=0;
 		fperiod=100.0/(mParams.p_base_freq*mParams.p_base_freq+0.001);
 		period=(int)fperiod;
+		// As getAudio bounds it: a looping sound restarts here at its
+		// envelope's end, and the next supersample divides by the period.
+		if (period < 8) period = 8;
 		fmaxperiod=100.0/(mParams.p_freq_limit*mParams.p_freq_limit+0.001);
 		fslide=1.0-pow((double)mParams.p_freq_ramp, 3.0)*0.01;
 		fdslide=-pow((double)mParams.p_freq_dramp, 3.0)*0.000001;
